## Why This Is Asked
Assesses practical data quality controls, schema evolution discipline, and safe deployment practices in multi-tenant streaming environments.

## Key Concepts
- Schema Registry with AVRO and compatibility enforcement
- Per-tenant schema namespaces and semantic versioning
- Real-time drift detection in Flink processing pipeline
- Automated quarantine and alerting mechanisms
- Circuit breaker patterns for data quality protection

## Code Example
```java
// Flink schema validation with drift detection
public class SchemaValidator extends ProcessFunction<GenericRecord, GenericRecord> {
    private final SchemaRegistryClient registry;

    @Override
    public void processElement(GenericRecord record, Context ctx) {
        try {
            Schema schema = registry.getLatestSchema(tenantTopic);
            if (!isValidAgainstSchema(record, schema)) {
                ctx.output(quarantineTag, record);
                alertDashboard("SCHEMA_DRIFT", tenantTopic);
            } else {
                ctx.output(validTag, record);
            }
        } catch (Exception e) {
            ctx.output(errorTag, record);
        }
    }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle non-breaking field removals while maintaining data lake query compatibility?
- How would you scale drift checks for high-throughput topics (>100K msg/sec)?
- What's your approach for schema evolution across multiple downstream consumers?

## Why This Is Asked

Test candidate's ability to design scalable security controls for multi-tenant K8s, covering RBAC, PodSecurity, image provenance, network isolation, and policy enforcement with Gatekeeper. Expect explanation of trade-offs (complexity vs. security) and how to validate in CI.

## Key Concepts

- Least privilege RBAC per-namespace
- Pod Security Standards
- OPA Gatekeeper constraint templates
- Image provenance and signed images
- NetworkPolicy segmentation
- Audit logging and policy testing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Test helper: ensures pods use allowed registries and non-root users
function isPodCompliant(pod){
  const okNamespace = pod.metadata.namespace.startsWith('team-');
  const okImage = pod.spec.containers.every(c => c.image.startsWith('registry.internal/'));
  const okUser = pod.spec.containers.every(c => c.securityContext?.runAsNonRoot === true);
  return okNamespace && okImage && okUser;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test Gatekeeper in CI/CD for new policies?
- How would you handle exception paths during incidents without breaking policy?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical array manipulation skills while maintaining sorted order, a common frontend data processing task. It evaluates understanding of efficient algorithms and the ability to work with constraints (no mutation, sorted inputs).

## Key Concepts
- Two-pointer technique for merging sorted arrays
- Deduplication by comparing with the last added element
- Time and space complexity analysis
- Non-mutating operations

## Code Example
```javascript
function mergeUnique(a, b) {
  let i = 0, j = 0, result = [];

  while (i < a.length || j < b.length) {
    let current;

    if (j >= b.length || (i < a.length && a[i] <= b[j])) {
      current = a[i++];
    } else {
      current = b[j++];
    }

    if (result.length === 0 || result[result.length - 1] !== current) {
      result.push(current);
    }
  }

  return result;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt this if inputs might not be sorted?
- What if we need to preserve the original order of first occurrence?
- How would this change for very large datasets that don't fit in memory?
- Could we optimize further if we know the range of possible tags?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical debugging of per-tenant feature flags and zero-downtime rollout strategies.

## Key Concepts
- Kubernetes ConfigMaps and pod configuration propagation
- Environment variables vs mounted files for configuration delivery
- Canary deployments and rollback safety mechanisms
- Observability practices and latency budget management

## Code Example
```javascript
// Reads a per-tenant flag from environment variable with fallback to false
function isBetaEnabled(tenantId){
  const cfg = JSON.parse(process.env.TENANT_FLAGS || '{}');
  return !!cfg[tenantId]?.betaRoute;
}
```
